--TEST--
a `private` property is not one of `T`'s keys, and a written-out name says so where it is written — `rule:types/property-key`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Vault {
    public string $label = "open";
    private string $secret = "shut";
}

// § 1's set is the *public* declared roster, and § 2 decides a written-out
// operand where it is written — so this never reaches a run, and the help
// names the whole set rather than only refusing this name.
property<Vault> $peek = "secret" as property<Vault>;
echo $peek as string, "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0405]: `Vault` has no public property `$secret`
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
